<title>UK: Blacks Leisure leaps higher on sales data.</title>
<headline>Blacks Leisure leaps higher on sales data.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Blacks Leisure Group Plc jumped 21-1/2p, or five percent, to 406-1/2p by 0845 GMT after the retailer reported like-for-like sales for the 44 weeks to January 4 1997 rose 22 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We're seeing some solid demand for the stock. It was a terrific result,&quot; one market maker said.</p>
<p>The company also said total sales rose by 45 percent while like-for-like sales at its First Sport retail chain increased by 22 percent over the previous year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
